---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="Planetary correlation lab" description="Explore relationships among the eight planets by plotting orbital and physical properties, changing axes and scales, and examining correlation.">
  <div class="container breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/tools/">Tools</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Planetary correlation lab</span></div>
  <header class="page-intro container">
    <div class="eyebrow">TOOL 07 · PLANETARY DATA</div>
    <h1>Compare planetary<br /><span class="heading-muted">properties.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Choose two properties and plot all eight planets. Change the axes or scale to see how the measurements relate.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section container data-lab">
    <div class="data-controls card">
      <div class="field"><label for="x-axis">Horizontal axis · X</label><select id="x-axis"><option value="distanceAu">Semi-major axis (AU)</option><option value="periodDays">Orbital period (Earth days)</option><option value="diameterKm">Equatorial diameter (km)</option><option value="massEarth">Mass (Earth masses)</option><option value="density">Mean density (g/cm³)</option><option value="gravity">Equatorial reference gravity (m/s²)</option><option value="eccentricity">Orbital eccentricity</option></select></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="y-axis">Vertical axis · Y</label><select id="y-axis"><option value="distanceAu">Semi-major axis (AU)</option><option value="periodDays" selected>Orbital period (Earth days)</option><option value="diameterKm">Equatorial diameter (km)</option><option value="massEarth">Mass (Earth masses)</option><option value="density">Mean density (g/cm³)</option><option value="gravity">Equatorial reference gravity (m/s²)</option><option value="eccentricity">Orbital eccentricity</option></select></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="axis-scale">Axis scaling</label><select id="axis-scale"><option value="log" selected>Logarithmic · both axes</option><option value="linear">Linear · both axes</option></select></div>
      <div class="data-controls-note"><span class="eyebrow">Explore</span><p>Try semi-major axis against orbital period first. Then compare mass with diameter, or density with gravity. The same eight planets can tell very different stories depending on the variables.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="data-results">
      <article class="card chart-card">
        <div class="chart-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Eight planets · two variables</span><h2 id="chart-title">Orbital distance vs. orbital period</h2></div><span class="tag" id="chart-scale-label">Log–log view</span></div>
        <svg id="planet-scatter" viewBox="0 0 680 450" role="img" aria-labelledby="scatter-title scatter-desc">
          <title id="scatter-title">Scatter plot of planetary properties</title>
          <desc id="scatter-desc">Eight data points, one for each planet, with a least-squares trend line. Choose different variables to redraw the plot.</desc>
          <g id="scatter-grid"></g><g id="scatter-regression"></g><g id="scatter-points"></g><g id="scatter-axes"></g>
        </svg>
        <div class="planet-legend" id="planet-legend" aria-label="Planet colour key"></div>
        <p class="chart-footnote">The dashed line is a least-squares fit in the currently selected coordinate scale. The coefficient describes linear association in that plotted space.</p>
      <p class="chart-footnote">Strength labels are descriptive rules of thumb. With only eight planets, do not treat this as a statistical test or evidence of causation.</p>
      </article>

      <aside class="card correlation-card" aria-live="polite">
        <span class="eyebrow">Live correlation</span><div class="correlation-value" id="correlation-value">+1.00</div><strong id="correlation-label">Strong positive relationship</strong><p id="correlation-note">The selected properties tend to increase together across these eight planets.</p>
        <div class="correlation-meter"><span id="correlation-meter-fill"></span></div>
        <dl class="correlation-facts"><div><dt>Planets plotted</dt><dd>8</dd></div><div><dt>Correlation coefficient · r</dt><dd id="correlation-exact">1.000</dd></div><div><dt>Scale used</dt><dd id="correlation-scale">Logarithmic</dd></div></dl>
        <div class="interpretation-note"><strong>Interpret carefully.</strong><p>Eight planets are a very small, highly selected dataset. Correlation is descriptive; by itself it does not establish causation or explain the underlying physics.</p></div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="card data-table-card">
      <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">The values behind the plot</div><h2>Inspect the data.</h2></div><p>Numbers are rounded reference values used by ORRERYA's planet profiles, not a new precision database.</p></div>
      <div class="table-scroll"><table class="planet-data-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Planet</th><th scope="col" id="table-x-heading">Semi-major axis (AU)</th><th scope="col" id="table-y-heading">Orbital period (Earth days)</th></tr></thead><tbody id="planet-data-rows"></tbody></table></div>
    </div>

    <div class="data-method prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Dataset notes</span><h2>Measurements used in this comparison.</h2>
      <p>The lab deliberately uses seven physical or orbital properties that can be compared across all eight planets. It does not pair a rocky planet's surface pressure with a gas giant's cloud-level reference pressure: those are not equivalent measurement surfaces. Likewise, giant-planet gravity is a reference-level value, not gravity at a solid surface.</p>
      <p>Mass is normalised to Earth's mass; density is mean density; gravity is the equatorial reference value. Semi-major axis and eccentricity use the full-precision JPL Table 2a elements referred to the J2000 mean ecliptic and equinox. Orbital period, diameter, mass, density and gravity use the reference values in ORRERYA's profile data, so the plot is an educational comparison rather than a homogeneous precision ephemeris dataset.</p>
      <p><strong>Reference sources:</strong> <a href="https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NASA NSSDCA Planetary Fact Sheet ↗</a> · <a href="https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/phys_par.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NASA/JPL Planetary Physical Parameters ↗</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { planets } from "../../data/planets";

    const palette: Record<string, string> = {
      mercury: "#aeb8c5", venus: "#e8bd91", earth: "#62a9d8", mars: "#d88368",
      jupiter: "#d6a77b", saturn: "#d7c18e", uranus: "#82c9c6", neptune: "#658fe0"
    };
    const metrics: Record<string, { label: string; unit: string; value: (planet: typeof planets[number]) => number }> = {
      distanceAu: { label: "Semi-major axis · J2000", unit: "AU", value: (p) => p.semiMajorAxisAu },
      periodDays: { label: "Orbital period", unit: "Earth days", value: (p) => p.orbitDays },
      diameterKm: { label: "Equatorial diameter", unit: "km", value: (p) => p.diameterKm },
      massEarth: { label: "Mass", unit: "Earth masses", value: (p) => p.mass1024 / 5.97217 },
      density: { label: "Mean density", unit: "g/cm³", value: (p) => Number.parseFloat(p.density) },
      gravity: { label: "Equatorial reference gravity", unit: "m/s²", value: (p) => p.gravityValue },
      eccentricity: { label: "Orbital eccentricity · J2000", unit: "", value: (p) => p.eccentricityValue }
    };
    const records = planets.map((planet) => ({
      slug: planet.slug, name: planet.name, color: palette[planet.slug],
      values: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(metrics).map(([key, metric]) => [key, metric.value(planet)])) as Record<string, number>
    }));
    const xSelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#x-axis");
    const ySelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#y-axis");
    const scaleSelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#axis-scale");
    const gridLayer = document.querySelector<SVGGElement>("#scatter-grid");
    const regressionLayer = document.querySelector<SVGGElement>("#scatter-regression");
    const pointsLayer = document.querySelector<SVGGElement>("#scatter-points");
    const axesLayer = document.querySelector<SVGGElement>("#scatter-axes");
    const ns = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
    const width = 680, height = 450;
    const plot = { left: 86, right: 646, top: 28, bottom: 365 };
    const plotWidth = plot.right - plot.left, plotHeight = plot.bottom - plot.top;

    function svg(name: string, attrs: Record<string, string>, parent: SVGGElement) {
      const node = document.createElementNS(ns, name);
      Object.entries(attrs).forEach(([key, value]) => node.setAttribute(key, value));
      parent.append(node);
      return node;
    }
    function format(value: number) {
      return new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { maximumSignificantDigits: 3 }).format(value);
    }
    function transform(value: number, mode: string) { return mode === "log" ? Math.log10(value) : value; }
    function inverse(value: number, mode: string) { return mode === "log" ? Math.pow(10, value) : value; }
    function mean(values: number[]) { return values.reduce((sum, value) => sum + value, 0) / values.length; }
    function pearson(xs: number[], ys: number[]) {
      const mx = mean(xs), my = mean(ys);
      let numerator = 0, xSquares = 0, ySquares = 0;
      xs.forEach((x, i) => { const dx = x - mx, dy = ys[i] - my; numerator += dx * dy; xSquares += dx * dx; ySquares += dy * dy; });
      return xSquares === 0 || ySquares === 0 ? 0 : numerator / Math.sqrt(xSquares * ySquares);
    }
    function correlationDescription(r: number) {
      const magnitude = Math.abs(r);
      const strength = magnitude >= .8 ? "Strong" : magnitude >= .5 ? "Moderate" : magnitude >= .25 ? "Weak" : "Very weak";
      if (magnitude < .25) return "Very weak linear relationship";
      return strength + (r > 0 ? " positive relationship" : " negative relationship");
    }
    function clearLayers() {
      [gridLayer, regressionLayer, pointsLayer, axesLayer].forEach((layer) => layer?.replaceChildren());
    }
    function update() {
      if (!xSelect || !ySelect || !scaleSelect || !gridLayer || !regressionLayer || !pointsLayer || !axesLayer) return;
      const xKey = xSelect.value, yKey = ySelect.value, mode = scaleSelect.value;
      const xMetric = metrics[xKey], yMetric = metrics[yKey];
      const title = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#chart-title");
      const scaleLabel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#chart-scale-label");
      const desc = document.querySelector<SVGDescElement>("#scatter-desc");
      const xHeading = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#table-x-heading");
      const yHeading = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#table-y-heading");
      const exact = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#correlation-exact");
      const value = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#correlation-value");
      const label = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#correlation-label");
      const note = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#correlation-note");
      const scaleOut = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#correlation-scale");
      const meter = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#correlation-meter-fill");
      const tbody = document.querySelector<HTMLTableSectionElement>("#planet-data-rows");
      if (!title || !scaleLabel || !desc || !xHeading || !yHeading || !exact || !value || !label || !note || !scaleOut || !meter || !tbody) return;

      if (xKey === yKey) {
        clearLayers();
        title.textContent = "Choose two different properties";
        desc.textContent = "The horizontal and vertical axes must represent different properties.";
        value.textContent = "—"; exact.textContent = "—";
        label.textContent = "Select distinct axes";
        note.textContent = "Comparing a property with itself always produces a trivial result.";
        meter.style.width = "0%";
        tbody.replaceChildren();
        return;
      }

      const raw = records.map((record) => ({ ...record, x: record.values[xKey], y: record.values[yKey] }));
      const points = raw.map((record) => ({ ...record, tx: transform(record.x, mode), ty: transform(record.y, mode) }));
      const xs = points.map((p) => p.tx), ys = points.map((p) => p.ty);
      const r = pearson(xs, ys);
      const minX = Math.min(...xs), maxX = Math.max(...xs);
      const minY = Math.min(...ys), maxY = Math.max(...ys);
      const padX = (maxX - minX || 1) * .1, padY = (maxY - minY || 1) * .1;
      const x0 = minX - padX, x1 = maxX + padX, y0 = minY - padY, y1 = maxY + padY;
      const mapX = (v: number) => plot.left + (v - x0) / (x1 - x0) * plotWidth;
      const mapY = (v: number) => plot.bottom - (v - y0) / (y1 - y0) * plotHeight;

      clearLayers();
      for (let i = 0; i <= 4; i++) {
        const tx = x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / 4;
        const ty = y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / 4;
        const gx = mapX(tx), gy = mapY(ty);
        svg("line", { x1: String(gx), y1: String(plot.top), x2: String(gx), y2: String(plot.bottom), stroke: "rgba(151,184,220,.13)", "stroke-width": "1" }, gridLayer);
        svg("line", { x1: String(plot.left), y1: String(gy), x2: String(plot.right), y2: String(gy), stroke: "rgba(151,184,220,.13)", "stroke-width": "1" }, gridLayer);
        const xt = svg("text", { x: String(gx), y: String(plot.bottom + 22), "text-anchor": "middle", fill: "#9aa9bd", "font-size": "10" }, axesLayer);
        xt.textContent = format(inverse(tx, mode));
        const yt = svg("text", { x: String(plot.left - 11), y: String(gy + 3.5), "text-anchor": "end", fill: "#9aa9bd", "font-size": "10" }, axesLayer);
        yt.textContent = format(inverse(ty, mode));
      }
      svg("line", { x1: String(plot.left), y1: String(plot.top), x2: String(plot.left), y2: String(plot.bottom), stroke: "rgba(196,213,239,.55)", "stroke-width": "1.2" }, axesLayer);
      svg("line", { x1: String(plot.left), y1: String(plot.bottom), x2: String(plot.right), y2: String(plot.bottom), stroke: "rgba(196,213,239,.55)", "stroke-width": "1.2" }, axesLayer);
      const xLabel = svg("text", { x: String((plot.left + plot.right) / 2), y: "425", "text-anchor": "middle", fill: "#d8e0eb", "font-size": "12" }, axesLayer);
      xLabel.textContent = xMetric.label + (xMetric.unit ? " (" + xMetric.unit + ")" : "");
      const yLabel = svg("text", { x: "19", y: String((plot.top + plot.bottom) / 2), transform: "rotate(-90 19 " + ((plot.top + plot.bottom) / 2) + ")", "text-anchor": "middle", fill: "#d8e0eb", "font-size": "12" }, axesLayer);
      yLabel.textContent = yMetric.label + (yMetric.unit ? " (" + yMetric.unit + ")" : "");

      const mx = mean(xs), my = mean(ys);
      let covariance = 0, variance = 0;
      xs.forEach((x, i) => { covariance += (x - mx) * (ys[i] - my); variance += (x - mx) ** 2; });
      const slope = variance === 0 ? 0 : covariance / variance;
      const intercept = my - slope * mx;
      svg("line", {
        x1: String(mapX(x0)), y1: String(mapY(slope * x0 + intercept)),
        x2: String(mapX(x1)), y2: String(mapY(slope * x1 + intercept)),
        stroke: "#f0d8a8", "stroke-width": "2", "stroke-dasharray": "7 6", "stroke-opacity": ".85"
      }, regressionLayer);

      points.forEach((point) => {
        const circle = svg("circle", { cx: String(mapX(point.tx)), cy: String(mapY(point.ty)), r: "6.5", fill: point.color, stroke: "#f3f1eb", "stroke-width": "1.3" }, pointsLayer);
        const tip = document.createElementNS(ns, "title");
        tip.textContent = point.name + " · " + xMetric.label + ": " + format(point.x) + (xMetric.unit ? " " + xMetric.unit : "") + " · " + yMetric.label + ": " + format(point.y) + (yMetric.unit ? " " + yMetric.unit : "");
        circle.append(tip);
      });

      title.textContent = xMetric.label + " vs. " + yMetric.label;
      scaleLabel.textContent = mode === "log" ? "Log–log view" : "Linear view";
      desc.textContent = "Scatter plot of " + xMetric.label + " against " + yMetric.label + " for all eight planets, with a least-squares trend line. Axis scaling is " + mode + ".";
      xHeading.textContent = xMetric.label + (xMetric.unit ? " (" + xMetric.unit + ")" : "");
      yHeading.textContent = yMetric.label + (yMetric.unit ? " (" + yMetric.unit + ")" : "");
      exact.textContent = r.toFixed(3);
      value.textContent = (r >= 0 ? "+" : "") + r.toFixed(2);
      label.textContent = correlationDescription(r);
      const orbitalLawPair = (xKey === "distanceAu" && yKey === "periodDays") || (xKey === "periodDays" && yKey === "distanceAu");
      note.textContent = orbitalLawPair && mode === "log"
        ? "This near-perfect log–log relationship is expected from Kepler's third law: T² is proportional to a³ for planets orbiting the same central mass. The high r is a known physical pattern, not a new discovery."
        : r > .25
          ? "The selected properties tend to increase together across these eight planets."
          : r < -.25
            ? "Higher values on one axis tend to accompany lower values on the other in this small dataset."
            : "There is little linear association between these selected properties across the eight planets.";
      scaleOut.textContent = mode === "log" ? "Logarithmic" : "Linear";
      meter.style.width = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.abs(r) * 100)) + "%";

      tbody.replaceChildren();
      points.forEach((point) => {
        const row = document.createElement("tr");
        const name = document.createElement("th");
        name.scope = "row";
        const swatch = document.createElement("span");
        swatch.className = "planet-swatch";
        swatch.style.setProperty("--planet", point.color);
        name.append(swatch, document.createTextNode(point.name));
        const xCell = document.createElement("td"); xCell.textContent = format(point.x) + (xMetric.unit ? " " + xMetric.unit : "");
        const yCell = document.createElement("td"); yCell.textContent = format(point.y) + (yMetric.unit ? " " + yMetric.unit : "");
        row.append(name, xCell, yCell);
        tbody.append(row);
      });
    }

    const legend = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#planet-legend");
    if (legend) records.forEach((planet) => {
      const item = document.createElement("span");
      const swatch = document.createElement("i");
      swatch.style.background = planet.color;
      item.append(swatch, document.createTextNode(planet.name));
      legend.append(item);
    });
    [xSelect, ySelect, scaleSelect].forEach((control) => control?.addEventListener("change", update));
    update();
  </script>

  <style>
    .heading-muted{color:#8796ad}
    .data-lab{padding-top:44px}
    .data-controls{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr .8fr 1.45fr;gap:18px;align-items:end;padding:22px;margin-bottom:17px}
    .data-controls .field{margin:0}
    .data-controls label{display:block;font-size:.75rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:7px}
    .data-controls select{width:100%;min-height:44px;padding:9px 11px;border-radius:5px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:#0a1220;color:var(--text);font-size:.79rem}
    .data-controls-note{border-left:1px solid var(--line);padding-left:18px}
    .data-controls-note p{font-size:.7rem;line-height:1.55;margin:7px 0 0}
    .data-results{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.35fr .65fr;gap:16px;align-items:stretch}
    .chart-card{padding:23px;min-width:0}
    .chart-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;gap:12px}
    .chart-heading h2{font-size:1.45rem;margin:8px 0 10px}
    .chart-card svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;overflow:visible}
    .planet-legend{display:flex;gap:12px 16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:2px 0 0;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.68rem}
    .planet-legend span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}
    .planet-legend i,.planet-swatch{display:inline-block;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;flex:0 0 auto}
    .chart-footnote{font-size:.67rem;color:var(--quiet);line-height:1.55;margin:14px 0 0}
    .correlation-card{padding:25px;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
    .correlation-value{font:600 clamp(2.7rem,5vw,4.2rem)/1 "Space Grotesk",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.06em;color:var(--gold-bright);margin:21px 0 9px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
    .correlation-card>strong{font-size:.92rem}
    .correlation-card>p{font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.65;margin:10px 0 18px}
    .correlation-meter{height:6px;border-radius:20px;background:#23334a;overflow:hidden}
    .correlation-meter span{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#82c9c6,#e6c88e);transition:width .2s}
    .correlation-facts{margin:21px 0}
    .correlation-facts div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:14px;padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:.73rem}
    .correlation-facts dt{color:var(--quiet)}.correlation-facts dd{margin:0;color:var(--text);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
    .interpretation-note{margin-top:auto;padding:15px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;background:rgba(9,18,31,.55)}
    .interpretation-note strong{font-size:.76rem;color:var(--gold)}
    .interpretation-note p{font-size:.7rem;line-height:1.6;margin:6px 0 0}
    .data-table-card{padding:25px;margin-top:17px}
    .data-table-card .section-head{margin-bottom:14px}
    .data-table-card .section-head p{font-size:.75rem}
    .planet-data-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:500px;font-size:.79rem}
    .planet-data-table th,.planet-data-table td{padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:right}
    .planet-data-table th:first-child,.planet-data-table td:first-child{text-align:left}
    .planet-data-table thead th{font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--quiet)}
    .planet-data-table tbody th{font-weight:600}
    .planet-data-table .planet-swatch{margin-right:9px;vertical-align:middle}
    .table-scroll{overflow-x:auto}
    .data-method{max-width:850px;margin:45px auto 0}
    .data-method h2{font-size:1.9rem;margin:11px 0}
    .data-method p{font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.8}
    .data-method a{color:var(--gold-bright);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
    @media(max-width:1000px){.data-controls{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.data-controls-note{grid-column:1/-1;border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:15px 0 0}.data-results{grid-template-columns:1fr}.correlation-card{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;column-gap:20px}.correlation-card .correlation-value{grid-row:2}.correlation-card>strong,.correlation-card>p{grid-column:1/-1}.correlation-facts,.interpretation-note{grid-column:1/-1}}
    @media(max-width:620px){.data-controls{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:17px}.data-controls-note{grid-column:auto}.chart-card,.correlation-card,.data-table-card{padding:17px}.chart-heading{flex-direction:column}.chart-heading h2{font-size:1.3rem}.correlation-card{display:flex}.data-method h2{font-size:1.6rem}}
  </style>
</SiteLayout>
